{
  "score": 32,
  "score_rationale": "SMCI carries deeply negative sentiment anchored by a cluster of analyst downgrades, massive insider selling, collapsing free cash flow, governance uncertainty, and a narrative that has shifted from AI darling to credibility-impaired value trap despite optically low valuation multiples.",
  "key_findings": [
    {
      "finding": "Analyst sentiment deteriorated sharply in late 2024, with JP Morgan, Barclays, and CFRA all downgrading in a 6-week window, leaving consensus at 'Hold' with zero Strong Buy ratings and the price target range ($26–$45) offering limited conviction.",
      "evidence": "[Source: FMP /analyst-ratings] — downgrades dated 2024-08-28 through 2024-09-06 from JPM (Overweight→Neutral), Barclays (Overweight→Equal Weight), CFRA (Buy→Hold)"
    },
    {
      "finding": "SVP Chief Business Officer Malyala Vikranth executed five separate sell transactions on 2026-05-21 totaling approximately $7.76M across a wide price range ($2.70–$45.32), signaling aggressive liquidation by a senior insider at multiple price points.",
